!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
As a directory
description: keyed children as named members, ordinal children as numbered ones
- >
  A container may be a directory ([directories](::language:concretes:storage:directories)): a keyed
  child becomes a subdirectory or file named by its key, recursively; an untagged ordinal child
  becomes a member under an order-numbered generated name (`item01`) plus a `- *: itemNN` pointer
  element in the parent's `body.yo` granting its position. A *tagged* ordinal container — a table, a
  typographical list — is content and stays inline in the body. The choosing rules are the
  [inheritance subchapter](::language:concretes:inheritance).
